Compatibility repair for an internally inconsistent pinned revision.

IDURAR is pinned at 5b2cf28969dc9a720c3fca20f0d2c7606534b277, which is a
mid-refactor commit that cannot create an invoice or record a payment through
its own UI — by anyone, human or agent. Two independent defects combine:

 1. backend/src/models/appModels/{Taxes,PaymentMode}.js were deleted, but
    backend/src/setup/setup.js still requires them and seeds a "Tax 0%" and a
    "Default Payment" default. The require throws MODULE_NOT_FOUND into
    setupApp()'s try/catch, which logs and exits — after Admin and Settings are
    created, so setup appears to succeed while the two defaults silently never
    exist. Worse, routes are generated from the model files present
    (backend/src/models/utils globs appModels/ into routesList), so with the
    models gone /api/taxes/* and /api/paymentmode/* are never registered at all.

 2. InvoiceForm.jsx's tax field was refactored from SelectAsync to Ant Design's
    plain Select while keeping every SelectAsync-only prop (entity, outputValue,
    displayLabels, withRedirect, urlToRedirect). antd's Select ignores them, and
    the field has neither `options` nor children — so it renders permanently
    empty under `required: true`. The now-unused `import SelectAsync` left at
    the top of the file is the fingerprint of the accidental swap.

Either defect alone makes the visible create-invoice flow unsubmittable; the
record-payment flow is blocked by (1) via PaymentForm.jsx's required
paymentMode SelectAsync. WebMCP arms are unaffected because their tools POST to
/api/invoice/create and /api/payment/create directly, which is why the
2026-08-18 failure audit saw every non-WebMCP configuration fail id-6 and id-7
(48 attempts) while every WebMCP configuration passed. That was an interface-
parity artifact, not a model-ability difference.

This patch therefore:
 - restores Taxes.js and PaymentMode.js verbatim from upstream a97c5f76, which
   re-registers /api/taxes/* and /api/paymentmode/* through IDURAR's own
   generic CRUD controller (no controller or route code is added), and lets
   upstream's own setup.js seeding run as written — so setup.js and reset.js
   are no longer patched at all;
 - restores the invoice tax field to the SelectAsync the file still imports;
 - keeps the /quote, /taxes and /payment/mode administration routes and
   navigation links removed, so those admin surfaces stay out of task scope.

No task, scorer, prompt or golden is changed. The repair can only raise
non-WebMCP scores and shrink WebMCP's measured advantage.

diff --git a/backend/src/models/appModels/PaymentMode.js b/backend/src/models/appModels/PaymentMode.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e7bd852
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/src/models/appModels/PaymentMode.js
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+const mongoose = require('mongoose');
+
+const paymentModeSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
+  removed: {
+    type: Boolean,
+    default: false,
+  },
+  enabled: {
+    type: Boolean,
+    default: true,
+  },
+
+  name: {
+    type: String,
+    required: true,
+  },
+  description: {
+    type: String,
+    required: true,
+  },
+  ref: {
+    type: String,
+  },
+  isDefault: {
+    type: Boolean,
+    default: false,
+  },
+  created: {
+    type: Date,
+    default: Date.now,
+  },
+});
+
+module.exports = mongoose.model('PaymentMode', paymentModeSchema);
